README.md:39:### 0.3.1-rc.3 release-candidate integrity
README.md:41:Successor to `0.3.1-rc.2`. Stops pinning stock dragon geo/anim (and egg geo) so Variant Loader / variant packs can remap those resources. Compile pin remains Forge 40.3.0. Promoted into 1.0.0.
README.md:44:File:   isleof-berk-performance-patches-0.3.1-rc.3.jar
README.md:49:### 0.3.1-rc.2 release-candidate integrity
README.md:51:Successor to `0.3.1-rc.1`. Widens the declared Forge range to `[40.3.0,40.4.0)` so live 1.18.2 Forge 40.3.x, including 40.3.12, can load. Compile pin remains 40.3.0. The immutable 0.3.0 release is unchanged.
README.md:54:File:   isleof-berk-performance-patches-0.3.1-rc.2.jar
README.md:77:The original Isle of Berk JAR and GeckoLib are required dependencies. The companion's common gameplay mixins should be installed with the same companion version on both client and server for multiplayer. Renderer and model mixins load on the client only.
README.md:81:1. Install Forge 40.3.x for Minecraft 1.18.2. The companion is compiled against 40.3.0 and accepts `[40.3.0,40.4.0)`.
README.md:84:4. For the published stable release, put `isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar` in the same `mods` directory. For the unpublished `1.0.1-rc.1` successor candidate, use `isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.1-rc.1.jar` from a local clean build and the successor manifest — not a renamed 1.0.0 jar. Install the same jar on both client and server.
README.md:86:6. For multiplayer, install the same companion version on the client and server.
README.md:88:The optional `isleofberk-deadlockfix` mod remains a separate artifact. Do not merge the JARs or treat this companion as a replacement for it.
README.md:95:- Twelve narrow client renderer argument-reuse transformations.
README.md:96:- Eight constructor-constant egg-animation and projectile fixed-resource transformations. Dragon geo/anim/texture and egg geo/texture remain uncancelled so Variant Loader can remap them.
README.md:99:These are narrow companion mixins. The original Isle of Berk behavior remains the source of all non-targeted logic.
README.md:120:- deadlock/safety/chunk-access behavior, including `getChunkNow` and `scratchPosDeadlockFix`;
README.md:121:- Variant Loader compatibility, taming, spawning, or world generation;
README.md:127:The historical Vonix waves through `1.2.1-vonix.13` were audited. The companion intentionally implements only the narrow, defensible subset documented here. See [CANDIDATE-REPORT.md](CANDIDATE-REPORT.md) for the wave-by-wave disposition.
README.md:131:The published 1.0.0 GitHub asset is the pre-cadence-conversion companion (`SHA256 15df9183...`). The current prerelease successor coordinate is **`1.0.1-rc.1`** with a distinct artifact filename and hash; bind identity from `CANDIDATE-REPORT.successor.md` and `evidence/candidate-manifest.json` after a successful local build — do not treat the historical 1.0.0 or 0.3.1-rc.1 JAR hashes as this successor.
README.md:136:- `auditPackagedJar`: companion-only archive; no bundled Isle of Berk or deadlock-fix content
README.md:166:The Vonix-owned companion source and metadata are MIT licensed. Isle of Berk and GeckoLib remain separate dependencies. This repository does not redistribute the Isle of Berk JAR.
