evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:34:    "artifact_package_scope": "Companion classes only; no com/GACMD implementation classes, deadlock-fix classes, duplicate entries, shaded dependencies, or unexpected resources found.",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:57:      "title": "Tests do not prove transformed interval, return-value, lifecycle, or constant-site semantics",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:64:      "causal_explanation": "AiMoveCadenceFixture tests only the pure modulo predicate. GameplayBytecodeFixture counts static invocation and bipush instructions but does not analyze branch exclusivity, calls per tick, whether moveTo's boolean result controls downstream behavior, or whether constants are the intended modulo divisors. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin classes rather than exercising a transformed WrappedGoal. The required original IoB JAR is absent from this frozen checkout, so those upstream fixtures are not independently reproducible here.",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:66:      "exact_repair": "Add an ASM-based target test that verifies control flow and return-value consumption, plus post-Mixin transformed-bytecode checks. Add an integration fixture covering zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; start/stop/restart; disabled and interval-1 modes; config reload; and long-lived counter behavior. Verify the egg and shock constants by their IREM/packet/damage dataflow, not only literal counts. Pin and record the tested IoB dependency digest."
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:97:      "causal_explanation": "CANDIDATE-REPORT.md identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a different JAR and digest, and 36 fixed-resource methods. The current tree is 1.0.0 and the current fixture covers eight fixed resources after Variant Loader compatibility removals. README explicitly labels much of its verification as historical and still lists the historical 36-method result.",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:98:      "impact": "Historical build/runtime success cannot establish that this exact HEAD and exact release JAR applied correctly or coexisted with current Variant Loader and deadlock-fix versions.",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:99:      "exact_repair": "Replace or clearly archive the old report. Produce a 1.0.0 report pinned to this HEAD/tree/JAR, with current eight-resource results, dependency digests, post-transform checks, and fresh client/server coexistence evidence."
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:117:      "title": "Variant Loader and deadlock-fix coexistence is structurally plausible but not tested for this release",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:123:      "causal_explanation": "Client classes are correctly confined to the client list, dynamic dragon and egg model/texture cancellations were removed, and the JAR does not bundle the deadlock fix. However, compatibility checks are source-string exclusions and upstream body checks. The twelve default-priority cancellable HEAD renderer injectors replace whole method bodies and no current multi-mod transformed-class or client runtime test is supplied.",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:124:      "impact": "No concrete collision was found, but same-method injections from another companion can be bypassed or conflict depending on priority and cancellation order.",
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:125:      "exact_repair": "Test the exact release with supported Variant Loader versions and the separate deadlock-fix JAR, capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence, and prefer a narrower invocation-level transformation where practical."
evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:132:      "repair": "Define and implement true tick-based AI cadence, then prove it against transformed pinned target bytecode and lifecycle/branch scenarios."
