evidence/sol-current-focused-verdict.json:1:{"schema":"sol-iob-performance-advisory-v1","verdict":"ADVISORY_REPAIR_REQUIRED","candidate":{"root":"/root/work/isleofberk-performance-patches","head":"515b9a677a39f72e9be12330355cbf765dbafcea"},"findings":[{"id":"SOL-001","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/config/PerformanceConfig.java","symbol":"shouldRunAiMove(int), shouldRunThrottledAiMove(int,int)","evidence":"The dirty edit removes both methods, but DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin:40, DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin:39, UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin:54, and AiMoveCadenceFixture:13-20 still call them. Java compilation therefore fails with unresolved symbols. The untracked AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings classes are not referenced by any active mixin.","recommended_fix":"Complete the cadence conversion atomically: migrate every caller and fixture to AiMoveCadence/PerformanceSettings, then remove the obsolete predicates. Do not restore the request-count predicate as a workaround.","required_tests":["Run a clean Java 17 `check build --offline --no-daemon --rerun-tasks` with the pinned dependencies and require zero compilation errors.","Add a source/bytecode gate rejecting calls to the removed PerformanceConfig predicates."]},{"id":"SOL-002","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin.java","symbol":"tick() redirects and vonix$resetAiMoveTick()","evidence":"Each active mixin still increments one int per redirected invocation and has no tick-HEAD decision. DragonFollowPlayerFlying has five redirected sites, so cadence remains invocation/branch dependent. Lifecycle hooks reset only that obsolete int. Skips currently return false through `&&`; AiMoveCadence.SKIPPED_MOVE_TO_RESULT=true is unreachable, and gateBoolean(boolean) cannot itself prevent eager evaluation of a navigation call. AiMoveCadence also retains an old cooldown when a reload changes one throttled interval greater than one to another.","recommended_fix":"Give each goal one bounded AiMoveCadence field; inject once at tick HEAD to call beginTick from one PerformanceSettings snapshot; make every redirect explicitly branch before invoking navigation, note an allowed request, and reuse the same decision for all sites that tick. Reset the cadence from WrappedGoal start/stop. Rearm deterministically when the enabled flag or effective interval changes. Remove or constrain gateBoolean so it cannot be used with an eagerly executed call. Prove original target return-value dataflow before selecting a skipped-call surrogate; if a consumed result has no behavior-preserving surrogate, defer that target.","required_tests":["State-machine test for zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; first eligible request; due ticks; disabled mode; interval one; interval changes; and more than 2^31 ticks with bounded state.","Instrumented redirect test proving skipped ticks execute zero navigation calls, allowed ticks preserve the original true/false result, and all calls in one due tick execute.","Post-Mixin transformed-bytecode test proving exactly one tick-HEAD decision and unchanged branch/RNG/target-selection structure.","Transformed WrappedGoal start/stop/restart test proving reset occurs at both lifecycle boundaries and the first later eligible request runs immediately.","ASM dataflow test for every pinned moveTo result; defer any site whose consumed result cannot be preserved."]},{"id":"SOL-003","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ADragonEggBaseMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ShockEffectMixin.java","symbol":"vonix$configureHatchCheckInterval(), vonix$configureParticleInterval()","evidence":"The active recurring injectors still call ForgeConfigSpec.IntValue.get() at lines 18 and 22. PerformanceSettings is written only by PerformanceConfig.refreshSnapshots and has no readers. Thus the claimed primitive hot-path snapshots are not implemented for AI, egg, or shock paths.","recommended_fix":"Read PerformanceSettings primitives in every active configurable mixin. AI should read enabled and interval once at tick HEAD; egg and shock should return their volatile primitive snapshots. Keep ForgeConfigSpec.get() confined to load/reload handling.","required_tests":["Forge config Loading and Reloading integration test changing all four keys and proving the next relevant tick observes them.","Foreign-spec event test proving unrelated ModConfig events do not alter snapshots.","Static bytecode test rejecting ForgeConfigSpec.get()/ConfigValue.get() calls from active mixin methods."]},{"id":"SOL-004","severity":"P1","file":"src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/AiMoveCadenceFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/GameplayBytecodeFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/MixinLifecycleFixture.java","symbol":"main() verification fixtures","evidence":"AiMoveCadenceFixture tests the removed modulo predicate and itself cannot compile. GameplayBytecodeFixture only counts invocations/literals in untransformed IoB bytecode. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin class shape. None proves tick decisions, transformed lifecycle execution, return-value consumption, reload visibility, or constant dataflow. The required IoB and GeckoLib JARs are absent from this checkout, so the Gradle JavaExec gates are not independently runnable here.","recommended_fix":"Replace the stale predicate fixture with direct AiMoveCadence behavioral tests; add ASM dataflow and post-transform fixtures against a digest-pinned IoB 1.2.0 input; exercise actual transformed WrappedGoal and goal ticks; provision dependencies in the verification environment without redistributing or editing them.","required_tests":["All cadence, lifecycle, return, reload, and long-run cases listed in SOL-002 and SOL-003.","ASM tests tying egg 20 to the hatch modulo and shock 8 to particle dispatch while proving damage 20 is untouched.","Record and verify SHA-256 values for the exact IoB and GeckoLib test inputs."]},{"id":"SOL-005","severity":"P2","file":"evidence/sol-deep-001/source-manifest.json; release-download/isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar","symbol":"files/head/tree manifest and packaged class identity","evidence":"The manifest pins the clean base tree and records PerformanceConfig SHA-256 56c0c8..., while the current file is 1d6fda.... It omits both new classes and already omits five tracked wrapper/git files. The inherited JAR SHA-256 15df9183... contains neither AiMoveCadence.class nor PerformanceSettings.class and therefore represents base v1.0.0, not this dirty candidate.","recommended_fix":"After repairs, commit a clean candidate, generate a complete manifest covering every tracked build input plus dependency digests, rebuild the reobfuscated canonical JAR from that exact commit, and bind report, tree, artifact name, size, SHA-256, and class inventory to one identity.","required_tests":["Verify every manifest entry and assert no tracked file is omitted without an explicit exclusion and digest.","Perform two clean builds from the pinned commit and require byte-identical JARs.","Run package, mapping, refmap, version, dependency-range, and class-inventory audits against the final artifact."]},{"id":"SOL-006","severity":"P2","file":"CANDIDATE-REPORT.md; README.md; config/isleofberkperformance.toml","symbol":"release identity, implemented surface, verification claims, AI cadence documentation","evidence":"CANDIDATE-REPORT identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a 47,478-byte JAR with SHA-256 7238b7..., and 36 fixed resources, not HEAD/base 1.0.0 or the dirty candidate. README verification still reports the historical 36-resource result despite the current eight-resource fixture. README:97 and the config fixture still describe later eligible-request intervals rather than one decision per goal tick.","recommended_fix":"Archive the historical report and generate a fresh report only after the candidate compiles and its final artifact exists. Update README/config comments to the tested goal-tick semantics and current eight-resource surface; include only exact, reproducible runtime and review evidence.","required_tests":["Documentation consistency gate comparing version, commit/tree, artifact SHA-256/size, resource count, mixin count, config defaults, and cadence wording with source and artifact.","Verify every referenced evidence path and digest exists and belongs to the final candidate."]},{"id":"SOL-007","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/resources/isleofberkperformance.mixins.json; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java","symbol":"client renderer mixins and Variant Loader exclusions","evidence":"The fixture only rejects selected source strings and checks original method bodies. Twelve active cancellable HEAD renderer injections replace complete getRenderType bodies. No fresh transformed-class or runtime evidence covers the exact final artifact together with Variant Loader and the separate deadlock-fix artifact.","recommended_fix":"Test the exact final JAR with digest-pinned supported Variant Loader and deadlock-fix JARs on client and dedicated server. Capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence and verify variant model, texture, animation, and egg remapping. If a collision is demonstrated, defer the affected optimization rather than editing Isle of Berk or silently weakening injector requirements.","required_tests":["Client launch with Isle of Berk 1.2.0, GeckoLib 3.0.57, Variant Loader supported versions, deadlock fix, and a deterministic variant pack; require correct remapped assets and no MixinApplyError/InvalidInjection/runtime linkage failures.","Dedicated-server launch with the exact companion and deadlock-fix artifacts; require all common mixins and config reload hooks to apply.","Export and inspect transformed classes to prove both companions' intended injections coexist."]}],"deferred_items":["Quantitative MSPT/FPS or allocation benefit is deferred until matched before/after profiling; egg and shock defaults provide no cadence reduction.","Any skipped-move boolean surrogate whose pinned target result is consumed is deferred until exact bytecode dataflow proves a behavior-preserving value.","Release and coexistence acceptance are deferred until a clean final artifact is built and tested."],"constraints":["Target remains Minecraft 1.18.2, Forge 40.3.0, Java 17, Isle of Berk 1.2.0, and GeckoLib 3.0.57.","Keep this a standalone companion; do not edit or redistribute Isle of Berk, merge deadlock-fix behavior, or weaken required injections into silent failures.","Preserve target selection, RNG order, combat/damage, progression, navigation algorithms, protocol, and lifecycle behavior except the explicitly reviewed cadence/performance changes.","Do not publish unsupported performance or compatibility claims.","Review was read-only; no files, artifacts, tags, releases, or external state were changed."],"acceptance":"NOT_ACCEPTED","effects":"NONE"}
evidence/sol-after-sol001.json:1:{"schema":"sol-iob-performance-advisory-v1","verdict":"ADVISORY_REPAIR_REQUIRED","candidate":{"root":"/root/work/isleofberk-performance-patches","head":"515b9a677a39f72e9be12330355cbf765dbafcea"},"findings":[{"id":"SOL-002","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/internal/AiMoveCadence.java","symbol":"beginTick(boolean,int)","evidence":"Tick cadence is now integrated, bounded, and one decision is reused per goal tick, but a live interval change between throttled values retains cooldownRemaining from the old interval. For example, after interval 20 arms cooldown 19, reloading interval 2 still skips up to 19 ticks; changing 2 to 20 can allow again after the old one-tick cooldown. PerformanceSettings also publishes enabled and interval through separate volatile writes and the mixins read them separately, so the AI tuple is not an atomic snapshot.","recommended_fix":"Publish the AI enabled/interval tuple atomically without per-tick allocation, read it once at tick HEAD, and have AiMoveCadence detect an effective setting change. On a throttled interval change, deterministically rearm so the next eligible request runs immediately and starts the new interval; document that reload rule.","required_tests":["State-machine test changing 20 to 2 and 2 to 20 during cooldown, asserting immediate deterministic rearm and subsequent spacing by the new interval.","Forge Reloading integration test proving one coherent enabled/interval tuple is observed on the next goal tick."]},{"id":"SOL-003","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ADragonEggBaseMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ShockEffectMixin.java","symbol":"vonix$configureHatchCheckInterval(int); vonix$configureParticleInterval(int)","evidence":"These active recurring handlers still call PerformanceConfig.EGG_HATCH_CHECK_INTERVAL_TICKS.get() and SHOCK_PARTICLE_INTERVAL_TICKS.get() at lines 18 and 22. This contradicts PerformanceConfig's claim that hot paths use PerformanceSettings primitives and leaves Forge config-object reads in every affected egg/effect tick.","recommended_fix":"Return PerformanceSettings.eggHatchCheckIntervalTicks() and shockParticleIntervalTicks() from the respective handlers. Confine all ForgeConfigSpec.get() calls to the spec-matched load/reload handler.","required_tests":["Static source and compiled-bytecode gate rejecting ForgeConfigSpec.ConfigValue.get() from every active mixin method.","Forge Loading and Reloading integration test changing all four keys and proving egg, shock, and AI observe the new snapshots; include an unrelated-spec event that must not change them."]},{"id":"SOL-004","severity":"P1","file":"src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/AiMoveCadenceFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/GameplayBytecodeFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/MixinLifecycleFixture.java","symbol":"main() fixtures","evidence":"AiMoveCadenceFixture now passes and tests the helper, but it does not invoke any redirect or transformed goal. GameplayBytecodeFixture only counts calls and literals in untransformed IoB bytecode, while MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin class shape. Direct inspection of the pinned IoB JAR shows all six moveTo results are immediately POPped and the two circle sites are mutually exclusive, but no deterministic regression test records that dataflow, constructor initialization of the new final cadence field, one transformed HEAD decision, zero skipped navigation calls, or actual WrappedGoal start/stop execution. The full clean gate has not passed; its latest attempt compiled main/test sources but later ended with StackOverflowError.","recommended_fix":"Add digest-pinned ASM and post-Mixin fixtures against IoB 1.2.0. Inspect and execute the transformed goal and WrappedGoal classes, including cadence-field initialization, while preserving required injector counts and original branch/RNG structure.","required_tests":["ASM test requiring POP immediately after all six pinned moveTo calls, IREM dataflow for egg 20 and shock particle 8, and unchanged shock damage 20.","Transformed/instrumented goal test covering zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick, proving skipped ticks call navigation zero times and due ticks execute every intended call.","Transformed WrappedGoal start/stop/restart test proving both reset hooks execute and the first later eligible request runs immediately.","Successful Java 17 clean `check build --offline --no-daemon --rerun-tasks` after the Forge build StackOverflowError is resolved."]},{"id":"SOL-005","severity":"P2","file":"evidence/sol-deep-001/source-manifest.json; settings.gradle; .offline-plugin-repo; release-download/isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar","symbol":"candidate build-input and artifact identity","evidence":"The manifest pins the clean base tree, records obsolete source hashes, omits AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings, and omits five tracked wrapper/git files. settings.gradle now gives an untracked 83-file local repository precedence, but those build inputs and their provenance are absent from the manifest. The inherited 32,865-byte JAR with SHA-256 15df9183a49e4d83a9d5e0583cec61a5a90549d873e5a64bb0116401988667e2 contains neither new helper class and is not this dirty successor; no completed successor JAR exists.","recommended_fix":"After source repairs, commit one clean candidate and generate a complete manifest covering tracked build inputs, wrapper files, pinned IoB/GeckoLib digests, and every local repository artifact actually consumed. Build and bind the canonical reobfuscated JAR, tree, version, size, digest, refmap, and class inventory to that identity; do not use unaudited untracked repository content as release provenance.","required_tests":["Manifest completeness and digest verification with explicit exclusions only.","Two clean builds from the pinned commit producing byte-identical JARs.","Package, mapping, refmap, dependency-range, version, and class-inventory audits proving AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings are present."]},{"id":"SOL-006","severity":"P2","file":"CANDIDATE-REPORT.md; README.md; config/isleofberkperformance.toml","symbol":"release identity, verification claims, and AI cadence wording","evidence":"CANDIDATE-REPORT still identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a 47,478-byte JAR with SHA-256 7238b7..., 36 fixed-resource methods, and unchanged predecessor bytecode. The successor changes gameplay bytecode and has no such artifact. README verification retains the historical 36-method result, while README and the deterministic config file describe later eligible-request intervals rather than one decision per goal tick.","recommended_fix":"Archive the historical report and create a successor report only after the final artifact exists. Update README/config wording to the tested tick-HEAD cadence and current eight fixed-resource surface, separating historical evidence from exact-candidate compile, transform, runtime, and review evidence.","required_tests":["Documentation consistency gate comparing commit/tree, version, artifact size/hash, class inventory, mixin/resource counts, config defaults, and cadence wording with the final source and JAR.","Verify every cited evidence path and digest exists and belongs to the final candidate."]},{"id":"SOL-007","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/resources/isleofberkperformance.mixins.json; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java","symbol":"client renderer mixins and multi-mod coexistence","evidence":"Client/common separation and removal of dynamic dragon/egg resource cancellations remain structurally sound, but the fixture only performs source exclusions and checks original IoB bodies. No fresh transformed-class or runtime evidence covers the successor artifact together with supported Variant Loader and the separate deadlock-fix JAR; twelve cancellable renderer HEAD injections still replace complete getRenderType bodies.","recommended_fix":"Gate the exact final artifact with digest-pinned supported Variant Loader, deterministic variant assets, and the separate deadlock-fix artifact. Capture transformed-class and runtime evidence; defer any demonstrated collision instead of weakening required injections or editing Isle of Berk.","required_tests":["Client launch proving variant model, texture, animation, and egg remapping with no MixinApplyError, InvalidInjection, linkage failure, or visual fallback.","Dedicated-server launch proving all common mixins and config load/reload hooks coexist with the deadlock-fix artifact.","Exported transformed-class inspection proving both companions' intended injections coexist."]}],"deferred_items":["Quantitative MSPT/FPS/allocation benefit remains deferred until matched before/after profiling; egg and shock defaults do not reduce their upstream cadence.","Release and coexistence acceptance remain deferred until a clean successor artifact passes the complete deterministic and runtime gates."],"constraints":["SOL-001 is resolved in this successor: all three goal mixins and the fixture use AiMoveCadence/PerformanceSettings, removed predicates have no callers, Java 17 main/test compilation and the targeted cadence fixture passed, decisions occur once at tick HEAD, state is bounded, and pinned moveTo results are discarded.","Target remains Minecraft 1.18.2, Forge 40.3.0, Java 17, Isle of Berk 1.2.0, and GeckoLib 3.0.57.","Keep a standalone companion; do not edit or redistribute Isle of Berk, merge deadlock-fix behavior, weaken required injections into silent failures, or alter target selection, RNG order, combat, progression, navigation algorithms, protocol, or lifecycle outside the reviewed cadence changes.","Do not publish unsupported performance or compatibility claims.","Review was read-only; no files, artifacts, tags, releases, or external state were changed."],"acceptance":"NOT_ACCEPTED","effects":"NONE"}
