evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2660:{"schema":"sol-iob-performance-advisory-v1","verdict":"ADVISORY_REPAIR_REQUIRED","candidate":{"root":"/root/work/isleofberk-performance-patches","head":"515b9a677a39f72e9be12330355cbf765dbafcea"},"findings":[{"id":"SOL-001","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/config/PerformanceConfig.java","symbol":"shouldRunAiMove(int), shouldRunThrottledAiMove(int,int)","evidence":"The dirty edit removes both methods, but DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin:40, DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin:39, UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin:54, and AiMoveCadenceFixture:13-20 still call them. Java compilation therefore fails with unresolved symbols. The untracked AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings classes are not referenced by any active mixin.","recommended_fix":"Complete the cadence conversion atomically: migrate every caller and fixture to AiMoveCadence/PerformanceSettings, then remove the obsolete predicates. Do not restore the request-count predicate as a workaround.","required_tests":["Run a clean Java 17 `check build --offline --no-daemon --rerun-tasks` with the pinned dependencies and require zero compilation errors.","Add a source/bytecode gate rejecting calls to the removed PerformanceConfig predicates."]},{"id":"SOL-002","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin.java","symbol":"tick() redirects and vonix$resetAiMoveTick()","evidence":"Each active mixin still increments one int per redirected invocation and has no tick-HEAD decision. DragonFollowPlayerFlying has five redirected sites, so cadence remains invocation/branch dependent. Lifecycle hooks reset only that obsolete int. Skips currently return false through `&&`; AiMoveCadence.SKIPPED_MOVE_TO_RESULT=true is unreachable, and gateBoolean(boolean) cannot itself prevent eager evaluation of a navigation call. AiMoveCadence also retains an old cooldown when a reload changes one throttled interval greater than one to another.","recommended_fix":"Give each goal one bounded AiMoveCadence field; inject once at tick HEAD to call beginTick from one PerformanceSettings snapshot; make every redirect explicitly branch before invoking navigation, note an allowed request, and reuse the same decision for all sites that tick. Reset the cadence from WrappedGoal start/stop. Rearm deterministically when the enabled flag or effective interval changes. Remove or constrain gateBoolean so it cannot be used with an eagerly executed call. Prove original target return-value dataflow before selecting a skipped-call surrogate; if a consumed result has no behavior-preserving surrogate, defer that target.","required_tests":["State-machine test for zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; first eligible request; due ticks; disabled mode; interval one; interval changes; and more than 2^31 ticks with bounded state.","Instrumented redirect test proving skipped ticks execute zero navigation calls, allowed ticks preserve the original true/false result, and all calls in one due tick execute.","Post-Mixin transformed-bytecode test proving exactly one tick-HEAD decision and unchanged branch/RNG/target-selection structure.","Transformed WrappedGoal start/stop/restart test proving reset occurs at both lifecycle boundaries and the first later eligible request runs immediately.","ASM dataflow test for every pinned moveTo result; defer any site whose consumed result cannot be preserved."]},{"id":"SOL-003","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ADragonEggBaseMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ShockEffectMixin.java","symbol":"vonix$configureHatchCheckInterval(), vonix$configureParticleInterval()","evidence":"The active recurring injectors still call ForgeConfigSpec.IntValue.get() at lines 18 and 22. PerformanceSettings is written only by PerformanceConfig.refreshSnapshots and has no readers. Thus the claimed primitive hot-path snapshots are not implemented for AI, egg, or shock paths.","recommended_fix":"Read PerformanceSettings primitives in every active configurable mixin. AI should read enabled and interval once at tick HEAD; egg and shock should return their volatile primitive snapshots. Keep ForgeConfigSpec.get() confined to load/reload handling.","required_tests":["Forge config Loading and Reloading integration test changing all four keys and proving the next relevant tick observes them.","Foreign-spec event test proving unrelated ModConfig events do not alter snapshots.","Static bytecode test rejecting ForgeConfigSpec.get()/ConfigValue.get() calls from active mixin methods."]},{"id":"SOL-004","severity":"P1","file":"src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/AiMoveCadenceFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/GameplayBytecodeFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/MixinLifecycleFixture.java","symbol":"main() verification fixtures","evidence":"AiMoveCadenceFixture tests the removed modulo predicate and itself cannot compile. GameplayBytecodeFixture only counts invocations/literals in untransformed IoB bytecode. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin class shape. None proves tick decisions, transformed lifecycle execution, return-value consumption, reload visibility, or constant dataflow. The required IoB and GeckoLib JARs are absent from this checkout, so the Gradle JavaExec gates are not independently runnable here.","recommended_fix":"Replace the stale predicate fixture with direct AiMoveCadence behavioral tests; add ASM dataflow and post-transform fixtures against a digest-pinned IoB 1.2.0 input; exercise actual transformed WrappedGoal and goal ticks; provision dependencies in the verification environment without redistributing or editing them.","required_tests":["All cadence, lifecycle, return, reload, and long-run cases listed in SOL-002 and SOL-003.","ASM tests tying egg 20 to the hatch modulo and shock 8 to particle dispatch while proving damage 20 is untouched.","Record and verify SHA-256 values for the exact IoB and GeckoLib test inputs."]},{"id":"SOL-005","severity":"P2","file":"evidence/sol-deep-001/source-manifest.json; release-download/isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar","symbol":"files/head/tree manifest and packaged class identity","evidence":"The manifest pins the clean base tree and records PerformanceConfig SHA-256 56c0c8..., while the current file is 1d6fda.... It omits both new classes and already omits five tracked wrapper/git files. The inherited JAR SHA-256 15df9183... contains neither AiMoveCadence.class nor PerformanceSettings.class and therefore represents base v1.0.0, not this dirty candidate.","recommended_fix":"After repairs, commit a clean candidate, generate a complete manifest covering every tracked build input plus dependency digests, rebuild the reobfuscated canonical JAR from that exact commit, and bind report, tree, artifact name, size, SHA-256, and class inventory to one identity.","required_tests":["Verify every manifest entry and assert no tracked file is omitted without an explicit exclusion and digest.","Perform two clean builds from the pinned commit and require byte-identical JARs.","Run package, mapping, refmap, version, dependency-range, and class-inventory audits against the final artifact."]},{"id":"SOL-006","severity":"P2","file":"CANDIDATE-REPORT.md; README.md; config/isleofberkperformance.toml","symbol":"release identity, implemented surface, verification claims, AI cadence documentation","evidence":"CANDIDATE-REPORT identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a 47,478-byte JAR with SHA-256 7238b7..., and 36 fixed resources, not HEAD/base 1.0.0 or the dirty candidate. README verification still reports the historical 36-resource result despite the current eight-resource fixture. README:97 and the config fixture still describe later eligible-request intervals rather than one decision per goal tick.","recommended_fix":"Archive the historical report and generate a fresh report only after the candidate compiles and its final artifact exists. Update README/config comments to the tested goal-tick semantics and current eight-resource surface; include only exact, reproducible runtime and review evidence.","required_tests":["Documentation consistency gate comparing version, commit/tree, artifact SHA-256/size, resource count, mixin count, config defaults, and cadence wording with source and artifact.","Verify every referenced evidence path and digest exists and belongs to the final candidate."]},{"id":"SOL-007","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/resources/isleofberkperformance.mixins.json; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java","symbol":"client renderer mixins and Variant Loader exclusions","evidence":"The fixture only rejects selected source strings and checks original method bodies. Twelve active cancellable HEAD renderer injections replace complete getRenderType bodies. No fresh transformed-class or runtime evidence covers the exact final artifact together with Variant Loader and the separate deadlock-fix artifact.","recommended_fix":"Test the exact final JAR with digest-pinned supported Variant Loader and deadlock-fix JARs on client and dedicated server. Capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence and verify variant model, texture, animation, and egg remapping. If a collision is demonstrated, defer the affected optimization rather than editing Isle of Berk or silently weakening injector requirements.","required_tests":["Client launch with Isle of Berk 1.2.0, GeckoLib 3.0.57, Variant Loader supported versions, deadlock fix, and a deterministic variant pack; require correct remapped assets and no MixinApplyError/InvalidInjection/runtime linkage failures.","Dedicated-server launch with the exact companion and deadlock-fix artifacts; require all common mixins and config reload hooks to apply.","Export and inspect transformed classes to prove both companions' intended injections coexist."]}],"deferred_items":["Quantitative MSPT/FPS or allocation benefit is deferred until matched before/after profiling; egg and shock defaults provide no cadence reduction.","Any skipped-move boolean surrogate whose pinned target result is consumed is deferred until exact bytecode dataflow proves a behavior-preserving value.","Release and coexistence acceptance are deferred until a clean final artifact is built and tested."],"constraints":["Target remains Minecraft 1.18.2, Forge 40.3.0, Java 17, Isle of Berk 1.2.0, and GeckoLib 3.0.57.","Keep this a standalone companion; do not edit or redistribute Isle of Berk, merge deadlock-fix behavior, or weaken required injections into silent failures.","Preserve target selection, RNG order, combat/damage, progression, navigation algorithms, protocol, and lifecycle behavior except the explicitly reviewed cadence/performance changes.","Do not publish unsupported performance or compatibility claims.","Review was read-only; no files, artifacts, tags, releases, or external state were changed."],"acceptance":"NOT_ACCEPTED","effects":"NONE"}{
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2733:    "artifact_package_scope": "Companion classes only; no com/GACMD implementation classes, deadlock-fix classes, duplicate entries, shaded dependencies, or unexpected resources found.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2756:      "title": "Tests do not prove transformed interval, return-value, lifecycle, or constant-site semantics",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2763:      "causal_explanation": "AiMoveCadenceFixture tests only the pure modulo predicate. GameplayBytecodeFixture counts static invocation and bipush instructions but does not analyze branch exclusivity, calls per tick, whether moveTo's boolean result controls downstream behavior, or whether constants are the intended modulo divisors. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin classes rather than exercising a transformed WrappedGoal. The required original IoB JAR is absent from this frozen checkout, so those upstream fixtures are not independently reproducible here.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2765:      "exact_repair": "Add an ASM-based target test that verifies control flow and return-value consumption, plus post-Mixin transformed-bytecode checks. Add an integration fixture covering zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; start/stop/restart; disabled and interval-1 modes; config reload; and long-lived counter behavior. Verify the egg and shock constants by their IREM/packet/damage dataflow, not only literal counts. Pin and record the tested IoB dependency digest."
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2796:      "causal_explanation": "CANDIDATE-REPORT.md identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a different JAR and digest, and 36 fixed-resource methods. The current tree is 1.0.0 and the current fixture covers eight fixed resources after Variant Loader compatibility removals. README explicitly labels much of its verification as historical and still lists the historical 36-method result.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2797:      "impact": "Historical build/runtime success cannot establish that this exact HEAD and exact release JAR applied correctly or coexisted with current Variant Loader and deadlock-fix versions.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2798:      "exact_repair": "Replace or clearly archive the old report. Produce a 1.0.0 report pinned to this HEAD/tree/JAR, with current eight-resource results, dependency digests, post-transform checks, and fresh client/server coexistence evidence."
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2816:      "title": "Variant Loader and deadlock-fix coexistence is structurally plausible but not tested for this release",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2822:      "causal_explanation": "Client classes are correctly confined to the client list, dynamic dragon and egg model/texture cancellations were removed, and the JAR does not bundle the deadlock fix. However, compatibility checks are source-string exclusions and upstream body checks. The twelve default-priority cancellable HEAD renderer injectors replace whole method bodies and no current multi-mod transformed-class or client runtime test is supplied.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2823:      "impact": "No concrete collision was found, but same-method injections from another companion can be bypassed or conflict depending on priority and cancellation order.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2824:      "exact_repair": "Test the exact release with supported Variant Loader versions and the separate deadlock-fix JAR, capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence, and prefer a narrower invocation-level transformation where practical."
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:2831:      "repair": "Define and implement true tick-based AI cadence, then prove it against transformed pinned target bytecode and lifecycle/branch scenarios."
