evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6394:CHANGELOG.md:9:- Same Mixin surface as `0.3.1-rc.3`: no stock dragon geo/anim pin, so Variant Loader / HybridsPlus / variant packs can remap those resources.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6395:CHANGELOG.md:17:- Stop cancelling dragon `getModelLocation` / `getAnimationFileLocation` (and do not pin dragon textures). Variant Loader 2.6.4/2.7.0 overwrites those lookups via `BaseDragonModelMixin`, per-species model mixins, and `ModelRedirectUtil`; a HEAD-cancellable stock `ResourceLocation` prevented variant geo/anim from applying and exploded remapped dragons.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6396:CHANGELOG.md:18:- Stop cancelling egg `getModelLocation`. Variant Loader remaps egg geo/texture through `DragonEggModelHelper`; egg animation remains constructor-constant and is still reused.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6397:CHANGELOG.md:19:- Keep the twelve renderer `getRenderType` argument-reuse mixins and the FireBolt/FuryBolt constructor-constant projectile mixins. Variant Loader does not remap those projectile methods.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6402:CHANGELOG.md:64:- The optional `isleofberk-deadlockfix` mod remains separate and is not bundled or replaced.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6403:CHANGELOG.md:66:- Network protocol, deadlock/chunk access, spawning, world generation, pathfinder algorithms, and dynamic resource selection remain outside this release.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6405:README.md:10:> **This is a companion, not a fork or replacement.** Keep the original `isleofberk-1.2.0.jar` installed. This project does not redistribute Isle of Berk classes or resources and does not include the separate `isleofberk-deadlockfix` mod.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6406:README.md:30:Successor to `0.3.1-rc.2`. Stops pinning stock dragon geo/anim (and egg geo) so Variant Loader / variant packs can remap those resources. Compile pin remains Forge 40.3.0. Promoted into 1.0.0.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6407:README.md:77:The optional `isleofberk-deadlockfix` mod remains a separate artifact. Do not merge the JARs or treat this companion as a replacement for it.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6408:README.md:85:- Eight constructor-constant egg-animation and projectile resource transformations. Dragon geo/anim/texture and egg geo/texture remain uncancelled so Variant Loader can remap them.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6409:README.md:109:- deadlock/safety/chunk-access behavior, including `getChunkNow` and `scratchPosDeadlockFix`;
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6410:README.md:110:- Variant Loader compatibility, taming, spawning, or world generation;
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6411:README.md:123:- `auditPackagedJar`: companion-only archive; no bundled Isle of Berk or deadlock-fix content
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6414:CANDIDATE-REPORT.md:42:- `vonix.5`: Partial. Fixed resources, renderers, and exact configurable flight movement cadence are implemented; deadlock/scratch changes remain excluded.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6415:CANDIDATE-REPORT.md:43:- `vonix.6`: Partial. Safe exact cadence surfaces are implemented; spawn, deadlock, and broad method-local rewrites remain excluded.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6416:CANDIDATE-REPORT.md:54:The release does not add `distanceToSqr` substitutions, deadlock/getChunkNow behavior, network-protocol changes, spawn/worldgen changes, shared static particle arrays, pathfinder algorithm substitutions, original Isle of Berk classes/resources, or deadlock-fix classes/resources.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6417:CANDIDATE-REPORT.md:63:- Prior production/SRG Forge runtime evidence still applies to the unchanged companion bytecode/entry contents (six common mixins applied; server reached `Done` without `MixinApplyError`, `InvalidInjection`, `InvalidInjectionException`, or `AbstractMethodError`). That run is not a hash pin for this reproducible artifact. Runtime evidence is limited to the unmodified `/root/iob-0.3.1-rc.1-production-gate-repair2-final/logs/latest.log` and `/root/iob-0.3.1-rc.1-production-gate-repair2-final/logs/debug.log`. `/tmp/iob-grok-0.3.1-rc.1-committed-runtime.log` is disqualified/invalid: it is contaminated by embedded worker prose and is not a complete raw console log. No replacement console log was fabricated.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6419:CANDIDATE-REPORT.md:77:- P3 contaminated console log: `/tmp/iob-grok-0.3.1-rc.1-committed-runtime.log` is disqualified/invalid and is not used as runtime evidence. Use only the unmodified `/root/iob-0.3.1-rc.1-production-gate-repair2-final/logs/latest.log` and `/root/iob-0.3.1-rc.1-production-gate-repair2-final/logs/debug.log`.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6422:evidence/sol-current-focused-prompt.txt:3:Known prior SOL findings: true tick cadence required; transformed behavior/lifecycle tests inadequate; repeated Forge config lookups in hot paths; stale CANDIDATE-REPORT; source manifest incomplete; no fresh Variant Loader/deadlock-fix coexistence test. Review exact current source, mixins, tests, Gradle files, metadata, and candidate report only. Check whether partial cadence changes compile and are integrated; verify all active mixin methods use reload-correct primitive snapshots; verify one decision per goal tick and return-value semantics; verify reset/lifecycle hooks; verify config reload behavior; inspect actual hot paths for allocations/config reads and bounded CPU changes; inspect manifests/provenance and artifact identity. Do not recommend workarounds, ARR base edits, gameplay/RNG/progression drift, silent failures, or unsupported performance claims. Preserve exact behavior except reviewed cadence/performance changes.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6423:evidence/grok-repair-001/brief.txt:5:Do not publish, push, deploy, restart, modify credentials, inspect unrelated workspaces, or claim acceptance. Preserve the repository's companion-only scope: do not bundle Isle of Berk or deadlock-fix classes/resources.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6425:evidence/grok-repair-001/brief.txt:16:F-004 P2: CANDIDATE-REPORT.md is stale and describes 0.3.1-rc.1/different commit/JAR/method counts. Replace/update it for exact current 1.0.0 HEAD/tree/artifact and current eight fixed-resource result. Clearly separate static evidence from runtime/performance evidence and do not invent fresh runtime evidence.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6426:evidence/grok-repair-001/brief.txt:20:F-006 P2: current 1.0.0 coexistence with Variant Loader and separate isleofberk-deadlockfix lacks fresh runtime evidence. Add only deterministic structural/package checks or documentation of required runtime gate; do not fabricate a runtime pass. Preserve client-only list and no bundled ARR/deadlockfix classes.
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6434:evidence/sol-current-focused-verdict.json:1:{"schema":"sol-iob-performance-advisory-v1","verdict":"ADVISORY_REPAIR_REQUIRED","candidate":{"root":"/root/work/isleofberk-performance-patches","head":"515b9a677a39f72e9be12330355cbf765dbafcea"},"findings":[{"id":"SOL-001","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/config/PerformanceConfig.java","symbol":"shouldRunAiMove(int), shouldRunThrottledAiMove(int,int)","evidence":"The dirty edit removes both methods, but DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin:40, DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin:39, UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin:54, and AiMoveCadenceFixture:13-20 still call them. Java compilation therefore fails with unresolved symbols. The untracked AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings classes are not referenced by any active mixin.","recommended_fix":"Complete the cadence conversion atomically: migrate every caller and fixture to AiMoveCadence/PerformanceSettings, then remove the obsolete predicates. Do not restore the request-count predicate as a workaround.","required_tests":["Run a clean Java 17 `check build --offline --no-daemon --rerun-tasks` with the pinned dependencies and require zero compilation errors.","Add a source/bytecode gate rejecting calls to the removed PerformanceConfig predicates."]},{"id":"SOL-002","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin.java","symbol":"tick() redirects and vonix$resetAiMoveTick()","evidence":"Each active mixin still increments one int per redirected invocation and has no tick-HEAD decision. DragonFollowPlayerFlying has five redirected sites, so cadence remains invocation/branch dependent. Lifecycle hooks reset only that obsolete int. Skips currently return false through `&&`; AiMoveCadence.SKIPPED_MOVE_TO_RESULT=true is unreachable, and gateBoolean(boolean) cannot itself prevent eager evaluation of a navigation call. AiMoveCadence also retains an old cooldown when a reload changes one throttled interval greater than one to another.","recommended_fix":"Give each goal one bounded AiMoveCadence field; inject once at tick HEAD to call beginTick from one PerformanceSettings snapshot; make every redirect explicitly branch before invoking navigation, note an allowed request, and reuse the same decision for all sites that tick. Reset the cadence from WrappedGoal start/stop. Rearm deterministically when the enabled flag or effective interval changes. Remove or constrain gateBoolean so it cannot be used with an eagerly executed call. Prove original target return-value dataflow before selecting a skipped-call surrogate; if a consumed result has no behavior-preserving surrogate, defer that target.","required_tests":["State-machine test for zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; first eligible request; due ticks; disabled mode; interval one; interval changes; and more than 2^31 ticks with bounded state.","Instrumented redirect test proving skipped ticks execute zero navigation calls, allowed ticks preserve the original true/false result, and all calls in one due tick execute.","Post-Mixin transformed-bytecode test proving exactly one tick-HEAD decision and unchanged branch/RNG/target-selection structure.","Transformed WrappedGoal start/stop/restart test proving reset occurs at both lifecycle boundaries and the first later eligible request runs immediately.","ASM dataflow test for every pinned moveTo result; defer any site whose consumed result cannot be preserved."]},{"id":"SOL-003","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ADragonEggBaseMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ShockEffectMixin.java","symbol":"vonix$configureHatchCheckInterval(), vonix$configureParticleInterval()","evidence":"The active recurring injectors still call ForgeConfigSpec.IntValue.get() at lines 18 and 22. PerformanceSettings is written only by PerformanceConfig.refreshSnapshots and has no readers. Thus the claimed primitive hot-path snapshots are not implemented for AI, egg, or shock paths.","recommended_fix":"Read PerformanceSettings primitives in every active configurable mixin. AI should read enabled and interval once at tick HEAD; egg and shock should return their volatile primitive snapshots. Keep ForgeConfigSpec.get() confined to load/reload handling.","required_tests":["Forge config Loading and Reloading integration test changing all four keys and proving the next relevant tick observes them.","Foreign-spec event test proving unrelated ModConfig events do not alter snapshots.","Static bytecode test rejecting ForgeConfigSpec.get()/ConfigValue.get() calls from active mixin methods."]},{"id":"SOL-004","severity":"P1","file":"src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/AiMoveCadenceFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/GameplayBytecodeFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/MixinLifecycleFixture.java","symbol":"main() verification fixtures","evidence":"AiMoveCadenceFixture tests the removed modulo predicate and itself cannot compile. GameplayBytecodeFixture only counts invocations/literals in untransformed IoB bytecode. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin class shape. None proves tick decisions, transformed lifecycle execution, return-value consumption, reload visibility, or constant dataflow. The required IoB and GeckoLib JARs are absent from this checkout, so the Gradle JavaExec gates are not independently runnable here.","recommended_fix":"Replace the stale predicate fixture with direct AiMoveCadence behavioral tests; add ASM dataflow and post-transform fixtures against a digest-pinned IoB 1.2.0 input; exercise actual transformed WrappedGoal and goal ticks; provision dependencies in the verification environment without redistributing or editing them.","required_tests":["All cadence, lifecycle, return, reload, and long-run cases listed in SOL-002 and SOL-003.","ASM tests tying egg 20 to the hatch modulo and shock 8 to particle dispatch while proving damage 20 is untouched.","Record and verify SHA-256 values for the exact IoB and GeckoLib test inputs."]},{"id":"SOL-005","severity":"P2","file":"evidence/sol-deep-001/source-manifest.json; release-download/isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar","symbol":"files/head/tree manifest and packaged class identity","evidence":"The manifest pins the clean base tree and records PerformanceConfig SHA-256 56c0c8..., while the current file is 1d6fda.... It omits both new classes and already omits five tracked wrapper/git files. The inherited JAR SHA-256 15df9183... contains neither AiMoveCadence.class nor PerformanceSettings.class and therefore represents base v1.0.0, not this dirty candidate.","recommended_fix":"After repairs, commit a clean candidate, generate a complete manifest covering every tracked build input plus dependency digests, rebuild the reobfuscated canonical JAR from that exact commit, and bind report, tree, artifact name, size, SHA-256, and class inventory to one identity.","required_tests":["Verify every manifest entry and assert no tracked file is omitted without an explicit exclusion and digest.","Perform two clean builds from the pinned commit and require byte-identical JARs.","Run package, mapping, refmap, version, dependency-range, and class-inventory audits against the final artifact."]},{"id":"SOL-006","severity":"P2","file":"CANDIDATE-REPORT.md; README.md; config/isleofberkperformance.toml","symbol":"release identity, implemented surface, verification claims, AI cadence documentation","evidence":"CANDIDATE-REPORT identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a 47,478-byte JAR with SHA-256 7238b7..., and 36 fixed resources, not HEAD/base 1.0.0 or the dirty candidate. README verification still reports the historical 36-resource result despite the current eight-resource fixture. README:97 and the config fixture still describe later eligible-request intervals rather than one decision per goal tick.","recommended_fix":"Archive the historical report and generate a fresh report only after the candidate compiles and its final artifact exists. Update README/config comments to the tested goal-tick semantics and current eight-resource surface; include only exact, reproducible runtime and review evidence.","required_tests":["Documentation consistency gate comparing version, commit/tree, artifact SHA-256/size, resource count, mixin count, config defaults, and cadence wording with source and artifact.","Verify every referenced evidence path and digest exists and belongs to the final candidate."]},{"id":"SOL-007","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/resources/isleofberkperformance.mixins.json; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java","symbol":"client renderer mixins and Variant Loader exclusions","evidence":"The fixture only rejects selected source strings and checks original method bodies. Twelve active cancellable HEAD renderer injections replace complete getRenderType bodies. No fresh transformed-class or runtime evidence covers the exact final artifact together with Variant Loader and the separate deadlock-fix artifact.","recommended_fix":"Test the exact final JAR with digest-pinned supported Variant Loader and deadlock-fix JARs on client and dedicated server. Capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence and verify variant model, texture, animation, and egg remapping. If a collision is demonstrated, defer the affected optimization rather than editing Isle of Berk or silently weakening injector requirements.","required_tests":["Client launch with Isle of Berk 1.2.0, GeckoLib 3.0.57, Variant Loader supported versions, deadlock fix, and a deterministic variant pack; require correct remapped assets and no MixinApplyError/InvalidInjection/runtime linkage failures.","Dedicated-server launch with the exact companion and deadlock-fix artifacts; require all common mixins and config reload hooks to apply.","Export and inspect transformed classes to prove both companions' intended injections coexist."]}],"deferred_items":["Quantitative MSPT/FPS or allocation benefit is deferred until matched before/after profiling; egg and shock defaults provide no cadence reduction.","Any skipped-move boolean surrogate whose pinned target result is consumed is deferred until exact bytecode dataflow proves a behavior-preserving value.","Release and coexistence acceptance are deferred until a clean final artifact is built and tested."],"constraints":["Target remains Minecraft 1.18.2, Forge 40.3.0, Java 17, Isle of Berk 1.2.0, and GeckoLib 3.0.57.","Keep this a standalone companion; do not edit or redistribute Isle of Berk, merge deadlock-fix behavior, or weaken required injections into silent failures.","Preserve target selection, RNG order, combat/damage, progression, navigation algorithms, protocol, and lifecycle behavior except the explicitly reviewed cadence/performance changes.","Do not publish unsupported performance or compatibility claims.","Review was read-only; no files, artifacts, tags, releases, or external state were changed."],"acceptance":"NOT_ACCEPTED","effects":"NONE"}
