evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6453:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:64:      "causal_explanation": "AiMoveCadenceFixture tests only the pure modulo predicate. GameplayBytecodeFixture counts static invocation and bipush instructions but does not analyze branch exclusivity, calls per tick, whether moveTo's boolean result controls downstream behavior, or whether constants are the intended modulo divisors. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin classes rather than exercising a transformed WrappedGoal. The required original IoB JAR is absent from this frozen checkout, so those upstream fixtures are not independently reproducible here.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6454:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:66:      "exact_repair": "Add an ASM-based target test that verifies control flow and return-value consumption, plus post-Mixin transformed-bytecode checks. Add an integration fixture covering zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; start/stop/restart; disabled and interval-1 modes; config reload; and long-lived counter behavior. Verify the egg and shock constants by their IREM/packet/damage dataflow, not only literal counts. Pin and record the tested IoB dependency digest."
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6456:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:97:      "causal_explanation": "CANDIDATE-REPORT.md identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a different JAR and digest, and 36 fixed-resource methods. The current tree is 1.0.0 and the current fixture covers eight fixed resources after Variant Loader compatibility removals. README explicitly labels much of its verification as historical and still lists the historical 36-method result.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6457:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:98:      "impact": "Historical build/runtime success cannot establish that this exact HEAD and exact release JAR applied correctly or coexisted with current Variant Loader and deadlock-fix versions.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6458:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:99:      "exact_repair": "Replace or clearly archive the old report. Produce a 1.0.0 report pinned to this HEAD/tree/JAR, with current eight-resource results, dependency digests, post-transform checks, and fresh client/server coexistence evidence."
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6462:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:117:      "title": "Variant Loader and deadlock-fix coexistence is structurally plausible but not tested for this release",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6463:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:123:      "causal_explanation": "Client classes are correctly confined to the client list, dynamic dragon and egg model/texture cancellations were removed, and the JAR does not bundle the deadlock fix. However, compatibility checks are source-string exclusions and upstream body checks. The twelve default-priority cancellable HEAD renderer injectors replace whole method bodies and no current multi-mod transformed-class or client runtime test is supplied.",
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6464:evidence/sol-deep-001/sol-review.json:125:      "exact_repair": "Test the exact release with supported Variant Loader versions and the separate deadlock-fix JAR, capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence, and prefer a narrower invocation-level transformation where practical."
evidence/sol-after-sol001.log:6513:{"schema":"sol-iob-performance-advisory-v1","verdict":"ADVISORY_REPAIR_REQUIRED","candidate":{"root":"/root/work/isleofberk-performance-patches","head":"515b9a677a39f72e9be12330355cbf765dbafcea"},"findings":[{"id":"SOL-002","severity":"P1","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/internal/AiMoveCadence.java","symbol":"beginTick(boolean,int)","evidence":"Tick cadence is now integrated, bounded, and one decision is reused per goal tick, but a live interval change between throttled values retains cooldownRemaining from the old interval. For example, after interval 20 arms cooldown 19, reloading interval 2 still skips up to 19 ticks; changing 2 to 20 can allow again after the old one-tick cooldown. PerformanceSettings also publishes enabled and interval through separate volatile writes and the mixins read them separately, so the AI tuple is not an atomic snapshot.","recommended_fix":"Publish the AI enabled/interval tuple atomically without per-tick allocation, read it once at tick HEAD, and have AiMoveCadence detect an effective setting change. On a throttled interval change, deterministically rearm so the next eligible request runs immediately and starts the new interval; document that reload rule.","required_tests":["State-machine test changing 20 to 2 and 2 to 20 during cooldown, asserting immediate deterministic rearm and subsequent spacing by the new interval.","Forge Reloading integration test proving one coherent enabled/interval tuple is observed on the next goal tick."]},{"id":"SOL-003","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ADragonEggBaseMixin.java; src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ShockEffectMixin.java","symbol":"vonix$configureHatchCheckInterval(int); vonix$configureParticleInterval(int)","evidence":"These active recurring handlers still call PerformanceConfig.EGG_HATCH_CHECK_INTERVAL_TICKS.get() and SHOCK_PARTICLE_INTERVAL_TICKS.get() at lines 18 and 22. This contradicts PerformanceConfig's claim that hot paths use PerformanceSettings primitives and leaves Forge config-object reads in every affected egg/effect tick.","recommended_fix":"Return PerformanceSettings.eggHatchCheckIntervalTicks() and shockParticleIntervalTicks() from the respective handlers. Confine all ForgeConfigSpec.get() calls to the spec-matched load/reload handler.","required_tests":["Static source and compiled-bytecode gate rejecting ForgeConfigSpec.ConfigValue.get() from every active mixin method.","Forge Loading and Reloading integration test changing all four keys and proving egg, shock, and AI observe the new snapshots; include an unrelated-spec event that must not change them."]},{"id":"SOL-004","severity":"P1","file":"src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/AiMoveCadenceFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/GameplayBytecodeFixture.java; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/MixinLifecycleFixture.java","symbol":"main() fixtures","evidence":"AiMoveCadenceFixture now passes and tests the helper, but it does not invoke any redirect or transformed goal. GameplayBytecodeFixture only counts calls and literals in untransformed IoB bytecode, while MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin class shape. Direct inspection of the pinned IoB JAR shows all six moveTo results are immediately POPped and the two circle sites are mutually exclusive, but no deterministic regression test records that dataflow, constructor initialization of the new final cadence field, one transformed HEAD decision, zero skipped navigation calls, or actual WrappedGoal start/stop execution. The full clean gate has not passed; its latest attempt compiled main/test sources but later ended with StackOverflowError.","recommended_fix":"Add digest-pinned ASM and post-Mixin fixtures against IoB 1.2.0. Inspect and execute the transformed goal and WrappedGoal classes, including cadence-field initialization, while preserving required injector counts and original branch/RNG structure.","required_tests":["ASM test requiring POP immediately after all six pinned moveTo calls, IREM dataflow for egg 20 and shock particle 8, and unchanged shock damage 20.","Transformed/instrumented goal test covering zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick, proving skipped ticks call navigation zero times and due ticks execute every intended call.","Transformed WrappedGoal start/stop/restart test proving both reset hooks execute and the first later eligible request runs immediately.","Successful Java 17 clean `check build --offline --no-daemon --rerun-tasks` after the Forge build StackOverflowError is resolved."]},{"id":"SOL-005","severity":"P2","file":"evidence/sol-deep-001/source-manifest.json; settings.gradle; .offline-plugin-repo; release-download/isleof-berk-performance-patches-1.0.0.jar","symbol":"candidate build-input and artifact identity","evidence":"The manifest pins the clean base tree, records obsolete source hashes, omits AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings, and omits five tracked wrapper/git files. settings.gradle now gives an untracked 83-file local repository precedence, but those build inputs and their provenance are absent from the manifest. The inherited 32,865-byte JAR with SHA-256 15df9183a49e4d83a9d5e0583cec61a5a90549d873e5a64bb0116401988667e2 contains neither new helper class and is not this dirty successor; no completed successor JAR exists.","recommended_fix":"After source repairs, commit one clean candidate and generate a complete manifest covering tracked build inputs, wrapper files, pinned IoB/GeckoLib digests, and every local repository artifact actually consumed. Build and bind the canonical reobfuscated JAR, tree, version, size, digest, refmap, and class inventory to that identity; do not use unaudited untracked repository content as release provenance.","required_tests":["Manifest completeness and digest verification with explicit exclusions only.","Two clean builds from the pinned commit producing byte-identical JARs.","Package, mapping, refmap, dependency-range, version, and class-inventory audits proving AiMoveCadence and PerformanceSettings are present."]},{"id":"SOL-006","severity":"P2","file":"CANDIDATE-REPORT.md; README.md; config/isleofberkperformance.toml","symbol":"release identity, verification claims, and AI cadence wording","evidence":"CANDIDATE-REPORT still identifies 0.3.1-rc.1, commit dcf712b, a 47,478-byte JAR with SHA-256 7238b7..., 36 fixed-resource methods, and unchanged predecessor bytecode. The successor changes gameplay bytecode and has no such artifact. README verification retains the historical 36-method result, while README and the deterministic config file describe later eligible-request intervals rather than one decision per goal tick.","recommended_fix":"Archive the historical report and create a successor report only after the final artifact exists. Update README/config wording to the tested tick-HEAD cadence and current eight fixed-resource surface, separating historical evidence from exact-candidate compile, transform, runtime, and review evidence.","required_tests":["Documentation consistency gate comparing commit/tree, version, artifact size/hash, class inventory, mixin/resource counts, config defaults, and cadence wording with the final source and JAR.","Verify every cited evidence path and digest exists and belongs to the final candidate."]},{"id":"SOL-007","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/resources/isleofberkperformance.mixins.json; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java","symbol":"client renderer mixins and multi-mod coexistence","evidence":"Client/common separation and removal of dynamic dragon/egg resource cancellations remain structurally sound, but the fixture only performs source exclusions and checks original IoB bodies. No fresh transformed-class or runtime evidence covers the successor artifact together with supported Variant Loader and the separate deadlock-fix JAR; twelve cancellable renderer HEAD injections still replace complete getRenderType bodies.","recommended_fix":"Gate the exact final artifact with digest-pinned supported Variant Loader, deterministic variant assets, and the separate deadlock-fix artifact. Capture transformed-class and runtime evidence; defer any demonstrated collision instead of weakening required injections or editing Isle of Berk.","required_tests":["Client launch proving variant model, texture, animation, and egg remapping with no MixinApplyError, InvalidInjection, linkage failure, or visual fallback.","Dedicated-server launch proving all common mixins and config load/reload hooks coexist with the deadlock-fix artifact.","Exported transformed-class inspection proving both companions' intended injections coexist."]}],"deferred_items":["Quantitative MSPT/FPS/allocation benefit remains deferred until matched before/after profiling; egg and shock defaults do not reduce their upstream cadence.","Release and coexistence acceptance remain deferred until a clean successor artifact passes the complete deterministic and runtime gates."],"constraints":["SOL-001 is resolved in this successor: all three goal mixins and the fixture use AiMoveCadence/PerformanceSettings, removed predicates have no callers, Java 17 main/test compilation and the targeted cadence fixture passed, decisions occur once at tick HEAD, state is bounded, and pinned moveTo results are discarded.","Target remains Minecraft 1.18.2, Forge 40.3.0, Java 17, Isle of Berk 1.2.0, and GeckoLib 3.0.57.","Keep a standalone companion; do not edit or redistribute Isle of Berk, merge deadlock-fix behavior, weaken required injections into silent failures, or alter target selection, RNG order, combat, progression, navigation algorithms, protocol, or lifecycle outside the reviewed cadence changes.","Do not publish unsupported performance or compatibility claims.","Review was read-only; no files, artifacts, tags, releases, or external state were changed."],"acceptance":"NOT_ACCEPTED","effects":"NONE"}
