ate. README verification still reports the historical 36-resource result despite the current eight-resource fixture. README:97 and the config fixture still describe later eligible-request intervals rather than one decision per goal tick.","recommended_fix":"Archive the historical report and generate a fresh report only after the candidate compiles and its final artifact exists. Update README/config comments to the tested goal-tick semantics and current eight-resource surface; include only exact, reproducible runtime and review evidence.","required_tests":["Documentation consistency gate comparing version, commit/tree, artifact SHA-256/size, resource count, mixin count, config defaults, and cadence wording with source and artifact.","Verify every referenced evidence path and digest exists and belongs to the final candidate."]},{"id":"SOL-007","severity":"P2","file":"src/main/resources/isleofberkperformance.mixins.json; src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java","symbol":"client renderer mixins and Variant Loader exclusions","evidence":"The fixture only rejects selected source strings and checks original method bodies. Twelve active cancellable HEAD renderer injections replace complete getRenderType bodies. No fresh transformed-class or runtime evidence covers the exact final artifact together with Variant Loader and the separate deadlock-fix artifact.","recommended_fix":"Test the exact final JAR with digest-pinned supported Variant Loader and deadlock-fix JARs on client and dedicated server. Capture applied-mixin/transformed-class evidence and verify variant model, texture, animation, and egg remapping. If a collision is demonstrated, defer the affected optimization rather than editing Isle of Berk or silently weakening injector requirements.","required_tests":["Client launch with Isle of Berk 1.2.0, GeckoLib 3.0.57, Variant Loader supported versions, deadlock fix, and a deterministic variant pack; require correct rem